WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.003
- All right, y'all.

00:00:01.003 --> 00:00:02.740
I save my favorite stories for the end

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:03.573
and this is a good one.

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:04.737
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.413
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.413 --> 00:00:08.370
(audience applauds)

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.450
All right, y'all. It seems like

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.660
everyone has a tequila brand these days.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.570
George Clooney, Dwayne
Johnson, Nick Jonas.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.570
But until recently,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.160
no tequila company was
owned by a black woman.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.190
That is until Nayana Ferguson.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.330
The Detroit native recently
launched Anteel Tequila,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.740
which is winning awards across the globe.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.200
She's also a cancer survivor,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.530
so let's get her in here.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.265
What's up, Nayana?

00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:31.930
(audience applauds)

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.490
- Hey, Kelly. How are you?

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.030
- I'm so good, and I love tequila,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.470
so we could be friends.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.980
So how did you get involved with tequila?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.730
- So, when my husband
Don and I started dating,

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.600
he was a tequila connoisseur,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.370
so he got me into drinking tequila.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.300
Later down the road,

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.440
when we were both looking
for a career change,

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.370
I asked him. I said, "If
you could do anything,

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.220
what would you do?"

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.520
And he said, "Open a tequila
company. But we can't do that."

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.320
And I said, "Why not?"

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.070
So a few days later, being
the businesswoman that I am,

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.720
I found a distillery.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.910
They sent us some samples
and we loved them.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.070
But we wanted to do things differently.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.790
So we created the world's only
coconut lime blanco tequila.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.844
- Yes.

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:20.690
- A Reposado tequila, aged
in Tennessee whiskey barrels.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.320
And they are both winning a lot of awards.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.720
We have two other expressions as well.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.720
- Oh, my gosh. That sounded amazing.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.840
So this part is incredible to me.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.498
You're also a pancreatic and
breast cancer survivor, right?

00:01:34.498 --> 00:01:36.145
(audience applauds)

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:37.050
- Yes, I am.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:37.890
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.410
And you're, you're healthy and
you're doing good now, right?

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.340
- Yes, I am.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.880
I am a 16 year pancreatic cancer survivor

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.560
and a nine year breast cancer survivor.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.490
At the time, I was a single mom,

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.710
and I knew I needed a positive mindset

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.500
to overcome those challenges.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.827
- Yeah. I also think
that had to make you go,

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:56.040
"No, we can do anything we want."

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.570
Look, this is, you have to take life

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.380
and really make it happen for yourself.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.710
I, I feel like that had
to, maybe, you said, "No."

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.150
Your husband was like,
"No, we can't do that."

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.060
And you were like, "We
could do anything we want."

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:05.893
I love that.

00:02:05.893 --> 00:02:08.099
I love that it kind of
pushed you, probably.

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:09.790
(audience applauds)

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.400
- Yes. Beating cancer twice

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.750
really changed my perspective on life,

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.530
and I knew if I could do that,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.850
I could overcome anything.

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:20.050
So when it came time to
creating Anteel Tequila,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.290
I knew it would be difficult,
but we can do this.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.620
- Yeah. We can do hard things.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.556
Thank you so much, Nayana.

00:02:26.556 --> 00:02:27.389
(audience applauds)

00:02:27.389 --> 00:02:29.507
I cannot wait to try your tequila.

00:02:29.507 --> 00:02:31.534
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.640
(bell sounds)

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.650
All right. And that's not all.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.630
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.930
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.910
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you, ma'am.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.990
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:44.840
How's that sound?

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.323
(audience applauds)

00:02:47.323 --> 00:02:48.239
- [Kelly] Yeah.

